* Week 7 — MITRE CAR analytics in Splunk SPL.
* Load data: Settings > Add Data > Upload > sysmon_proc.json, sourcetype=_json, index=th_proc.
* (On a real host these fields come from Sysmon EventID 1 via the Splunk Add-on for Sysmon.)

* ===========================================================================
* CAR-2013-02-003 — Processes Spawning cmd.exe  ->  ATT&CK T1059.003
* Phishing-attachment variant: an Office/mail/PDF app spawning cmd.exe means a
* malicious document was opened (CAR's own description names Outlook/Adobe Reader).
* ===========================================================================
index=th_proc sourcetype=_json event_id=1 process_name=cmd.exe
  parent_process_name IN (outlook.exe, winword.exe, excel.exe, powerpnt.exe, acrord32.exe)
| table _time, host, user, parent_process_name, process_name, command_line
| sort _time

* Real Sysmon field names (if using the TA):
* source="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=1
*   Image="*\\cmd.exe" (ParentImage="*\\outlook.exe" OR ParentImage="*\\winword.exe" ...)

* ===========================================================================
* CAR-2014-04-003 — PowerShell Execution  ->  ATT&CK T1059.001
* v1 (literal CAR pseudocode): parent != explorer.exe  -> too noisy in our org.
* v2 (tuned): add the encoded / hidden-window discriminator.
* ===========================================================================
* v1 (shown to demonstrate alert fatigue — do NOT deploy as-is):
index=th_proc sourcetype=_json event_id=1 process_name=powershell.exe parent_process_name!=explorer.exe
| stats count BY host

* v2 (deploy this):
index=th_proc sourcetype=_json event_id=1 process_name=powershell.exe parent_process_name!=explorer.exe
  (command_line="*-enc*" OR command_line="*hidden*")
| table _time, host, user, parent_process_name, command_line
| sort _time
